sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/altitude-coupling> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Demand rises and supply falls with height together, so the flyable heights reach down to the ground (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "In an atmosphere where air density and oxygen partial pressure both fall with height, the minimum speed of lift-supported flight and the power to fly at it rise with height while the aerobic supply falls, so flight possible at a height is possible at every lower height, infeasibility propagates upward, and a design that cannot fly at the ground cannot fly at any height. The direction is proved; the size of the effect is data and it is gentle." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Favored.lean) as an extension of the neutral case of Kimura (1962) to non-opposing selection; no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "h1 ≤ h2 and feasible(h2) implies feasible(h1); not feasible(0) implies not feasible(h) for all h ≥ 0" ;
    skos:definition """/-- **The minimum speed rises with height.** -/
theorem vmin_mono {W S CL : ℝ} (hW : 0 < W) (hS : 0 < S) (hCL : 0 < CL) {h₁ h₂ : ℝ} (h : h₁ ≤ h₂) :
    vminAt A W S CL h₁ ≤ vminAt A W S CL h₂"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.Altitude.Atmosphere" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.Altitude.vmin_mono", "Delphi.Altitude.demand_mono", "Delphi.Altitude.supply_anti", "Delphi.Altitude.feasible_downward_closed", "Delphi.Altitude.ceiling", "Delphi.Altitude.infeasible_at_ground_infeasible_everywhere" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "The DIRECTION of the effect is proved; its SIZE is data and it is gentle (about 30% more required capacity from 0 to 5000 m, arterial content 0.190 to 0.173 ml/ml), and the real fish sits more than thirty times below every boundary at every height. So nothing here supports reading \"the feasible region shrinks with altitude\" as the reason a fish cannot fly high: the reason is the oxygen budget at sea level. Compensation an animal might make at altitude (haematocrit, ventilation, cardiac output) is held fixed, and no bird data is used. The declaration in delphi:leanDeclaration (Delphi.Altitude.Atmosphere) is a NAMED HYPOTHESIS this theorem takes as an argument, not a definition the law rests on: it is a monotone atmosphere: that air density and oxygen partial pressure both fall with height, so the premise must not be read as the law." ;

    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: A monotone atmosphere: both density and oxygen partial pressure fall with height. No profile, no numbers; the candidates' profile is the physics thread's NASA Glenn fit; Arterial content nondecreasing in partial pressure (a Hill curve is, but the Hill equation, the Bohr shift and the Root effect are not formalised); Everything else held fixed with height: the animal makes no compensation (haematocrit, ventilation, cardiac output), and temperature, humidity and wind are outside the model; The size of the effect is NOT proved: it is gentle, and the binding constraint for the real fish is the aerobic ceiling at sea level. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Altitude.lean>, <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/altitude-coupling> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/altitude-coupling> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-altitude-coupling> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-altitude-coupling> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.Altitude.vmin_mono with zero sorry and standard axioms; it also rejected 1 deliberately broken variant(s) of this statement or its model" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.3 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Altitude.lean (152 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.Altitude.vmin_mono, Delphi.Altitude.demand_mono, Delphi.Altitude.supply_anti, Delphi.Altitude.feasible_downward_closed, Delphi.Altitude.ceiling, Delphi.Altitude.infeasible_at_ground_infeasible_everywhere: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T22:57:06.367Z): 1 deliberate change(s) to this statement or its model were each rejected by the compiler: [altitude-feasible-upward-closed] Statement reversed: feasibility at a height claimed to carry UPWARD (to every greater height) instead of downward. That is the opposite of what thinning air and falling oxygen give, and it would turn a ceiling into a floor, so the proof must fail. Rejected with 4 error(s): Altitude.lean:112:36: error: Type mismatch Controls: 17 of 17 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/altitude-coupling> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: A monotone atmosphere: both density and oxygen partial pressure fall with height. No profile, no numbers; the candidates' profile is the physics thread's NASA Glenn fit; Arterial content nondecreasing in partial pressure (a Hill curve is, but the Hill equation, the Bohr shift and the Root effect are not formalised); Everything else held fixed with height: the animal makes no compensation (haematocrit, ventilation, cardiac output), and temperature, humidity and wind are outside the model; The size of the effect is NOT proved: it is gentle, and the binding constraint for the real fish is the aerobic ceiling at sea level. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

